=== MODIFIER ic
Continuation (item)
A spell stuck in a przemdiot will be triggered when there is energy for it.
:ik

=== MODIFIER im1
Reduced energy expenditure of the item
The cost of the spell in the item is reduced.
M-

=== MODIFIER im2
Minimal energy expenditure of the item
The cost of the spell in the item is greatly reduced.
M--

=== MODIFIER ir1
Item energy regeneration
Increases the energy regeneration rate of the item with the spell.
R+

=== MODIFIER ir2
Fast item energy regeneration
Significantly increases the energy regeneration rate of the item with the spell.
R++

=== MODIFIER it
Triggered Action (Item)
A spell stuck in an item will take effect when the item is used.
:Iw

=== MODIFIER m1
Reduced energy
The energy required to cast the spell will be reduced.
E-

=== MODIFIER m2
Minimal energy
The energy required to cast the spell will be greatly reduced.
E--

=== MODIFIER r0
Half Increased Range
The original maximum range of casting this spell will increase by half.
-Z+

=== MODIFIER r1
Increased Range
The original maximum range of casting this spell will double.
Z+

=== MODIFIER r2
Maximum Range
The original maximum range of casting this spell will triple.
Z++

=== MODIFIER t1
Additional target
In addition to the selected target, the spell will work on another nearby target.
C+

=== MODIFIER t2
Additional targets
In addition to the selected target, the spell will work on two more nearby targets.
C++

